Subject: [PATCH] GS read-back ahead: the capture already taken, without
 waiting

A small region read back every frame (Transformers' 64 x 64 lens-flare occlusion buffer) held the EE until the GS thread reached it; a frame that missed its VBlank by that wait lost a whole frame. It is now answered from the capture already taken (the frame before's). PS2X_READBACK_STALE=0: wait as before.
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_threaded_backend.cpp | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_threaded_backend.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_threaded_backend.cpp
index 3cdcb5b..1ea2393 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_threaded_backend.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_threaded_backend.cpp
@@ -321,7 +321,18 @@ bool GSThreadedBackend::ReadbackAhead(const GSTransferCommand &command, uint8_t
         m_readbackPending = false;
         publish();
     }
-    waitCaptured(position, captureNumber);
+    // The capture already taken (the frame before's, as a rule) without waiting for this one: a
+    // small region read back every frame - Transformers' 64 x 64 occlusion buffer for its lens
+    // flares' visibility - otherwise holds the EE until the GS thread gets to it, and a frame that
+    // misses its VBlank by that wait loses a whole frame (Deep Amazon replayed: a quarter fewer
+    // such frames). PS2X_READBACK_STALE=0: wait for this frame's, as before.
+    static const bool stale = []()
+    {
+        const char *env = std::getenv("PS2X_READBACK_STALE");
+        return !(env && *env == '0');
+    }();
+    if (!stale || m_capturesTaken.load(std::memory_order_acquire) == 0u)
+        waitCaptured(position, captureNumber);
     {
         std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m_captureMutex);
         bytes = std::min(maxBytes, m_capturedBytes);
